  "body": "Add standard 3-axis `.mch` machine files for the Brother Speedio S500X2 and S700X2 using verified Brother X2 specifications.\n\n## Scope\n- Add `assets/machines/brother-s500x2.mch`: `X 500`, `Y 400`, `Z 300` mm travel (`safe_retract` at top), table `600 x 400` mm, spindle-nose to table `180–480` mm, `14`-tool ATC.\n- Add `assets/machines/brother-s700x2.mch`: `X 700`, `Y 400`, `Z 300` mm travel (`safe_retract` at top), table `800 x 400` mm, spindle-nose to table `180–480` mm, `14`-tool ATC.\n- Set common Speedio X2 specs on both files: `\"vendor\": \"Camcraft\"`, `\"spindle_mount\": \"BT30\"`, `\"default_holder\": \"BT30 ER20\"`, `\"mount_source\"` (`global.brother` URL), spindle `1–10,000` rpm (`7.1` kW continuous, `rigid_tapping: true`), rapid `X/Y 50,000`, `Z 56,000` mm/min, max feed `30,000` mm/min.\n- Declare Brother coolants (`Flood` `M8`, `Air` `M458`, `Through-Spindle` `M494`) and verify pure JSON syntax (no comments in `.mch` files).\n- Register both machines in `MACHINES` (`crates/app/src/posting.rs`), pair with `brother-speedio.cps`, and add unit tests matching `crates/app/tests/tormach_machines.rs`.\n\nDone means: `brother-s500x2.mch` and `brother-s700x2.mch` are registered in `MACHINES`, pair with `brother-speedio.cps`, pass `every_shipped_machine_mounts_and_speaks_its_declaration` (`crates/app/tests/machine.rs`), and pass dedicated spec pinning tests.\n\nPart of #1960\n",
